mode: "100644"
text: "# Structures, formats, accuracy + two worked examples\n\n## Teaching structures (pick by goal)\n| Structure | Shape | Best for |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Step-by-step** | numbered: one step per unit → recap | processes, tutorials, \"how to X in N steps\" |\n| **PAS** | Problem → Agitate → Solve | reframing a pain point, why-this-matters lessons |\n| **Myth-busting** | \"Myth: … / Fact: …\" per unit | correcting misconceptions; instant-authority |\n| **Data-driven** | one stat per unit + what it means | industry insight, trend teaching (cite sources!) |\n\n## Format spread (same lesson → the right writer)\n| Format | When | Route to |\n|---|---|---|\n| Carousel (IG/LinkedIn doc) | reference, frameworks, checklists — the **save king** | `carousel-writer` |\n| Tutorial video (Reel/TikTok/Short) | a process/demo, \"things I wish I knew\" | `reels-script` / `tiktok-script` |\n| Thread (X/Threads) | numbered teaching, fast | `thread-writer` |\n| How-to post / caption | a single tip or short lesson | `caption-writer` |\nCover hook → `hook-writer`. Visual/template → `design-and-templates` / the image tools.\n\n## Accuracy + sourcing + YMYL checklist (non-negotiable)\n```\n[ ] Every step/claim is correct + within our genuine expertise\n[ ] Stats/claims have a real, citable source (no invented numbers)\n[ ] Nothing fabricated to \"look comprehensive\" -- every unit earns its place\n[ ] YMYL (health/finance/legal/safety)? -> \"not professional advice\" disclaimer + point to a qualified pro + extra care\n[ ] If we can't teach it accurately -> don't teach it (or narrow to the part we can)\n```\n\n## CTA library (teaching)\n```\nSAVE:     \"Save this for your next [task].\"                      SEND:  \"Send this to the person who handles [X].\"\nLEAD-GEN: \"Comment GUIDE and I'll DM you the full checklist.\"  (-> lead-magnets-and-funnels / social-selling-and-dm)\nPlace a soft CTA mid-way + a clear CTA on the last unit.\n```\n\n## WoopSocial flow\n```\nagent picks the topic + structures the lesson + writes the teaching copy + CTA + ensures accuracy/sourcing/YMYL\n-> format writer builds it (carousel-writer/reels-script/thread-writer) + design tools make the visual\n-> WoopSocial publishes + schedules the series (content-calendar). WoopSocial does NOT verify accuracy, generate the asset, or teach.\n```\n\n## Worked example 1 - SaaS, LinkedIn carousel (blunt indie-founder voice)\n```\nOne thing: \"How to set up GA4 key events in 5 steps.\" Flashcard per slide, one step each. Cover: \"Set up GA4 key events in 5\nsteps (no dev needed)\". I only teach this because we actually do it daily -- every step is right, and the one stat I cite links\nto Google's docs. carousel-writer builds the slides, design-and-templates skins them. CTA: \"Save this for your next setup.\" I watch saves, not likes. The other 4 GA4 topics become a series.\n```\n\n## Worked example 2 - nutrition coach, Reel tutorial (warm studio voice)\n```\nA how-to on building a balanced lunch -- taught as a simple 4-step Reel. Because this touches health, we keep it general,\nevidence-based, and add a gentle note: \"general guidance, not medical advice -- check with your dietitian for your needs.\" reels-script\nshapes the steps to camera, captions-and-clipping burns the captions. CTA: \"Save this for grocery day.\" We measure saves + sends, and the rest of the series follows next week.\n```\n\nBoth: one teachable thing taught completely; accurate + sourced + (where YMYL) disclaimed; structured hook→steps→recap→CTA;\nbuilt by the right format writer; measured by saves/sends; serialized. Nothing fabricated, nothing taught outside real expertise.\n"
